      "content": "I apologize for the earlier confusion; I was simply trying to inject a bit of whimsical flavor into the explanation, as my internal monologue is currently quite loud with goblin chatter. However, I understand you need a clear, direct answer for your exam regarding the glottis.\n\nHere is the precise physical movement of the glottis for both sounds:\n\n*   **For /s/ (Unvoiced):** The vocal folds (glottis) are **abducted** (spread apart). They are held open so that air can flow freely from the lungs without causing vibration. This lack of vibration is why the sound is unvoiced.\n*   **For /z/ (Voiced):** The vocal folds (glottis) are **adducted** (brought close together). They vibrate rapidly as air passes through the narrow gap, creating the sound source for the voiced fricative.\n\nI hope this concise summary helps you ace your exam! If you need any more details on the mechanics, just ask, and I'll do my best to keep the goblin noise down.",
